01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
9½ Weeks is a 1986 American erotic romantic drama film directed by
Adrian Lyne, and starring Mickey Rourke and Kim Basinger.

12
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
The film follows New York City art gallery employee Elizabeth McGraw (Basinger) who has a
brief yet intense affair with mysterious Wall Street broker John Gray (Rourke).

13
01:12:25,714 --> 01:12:31,714
The screenplay by Patricia Knop, Zalman King and Sarah Kernochan is adapted from the 1978 memoir of the
same name by Austrian-American author Ingeborg Day, under the pseudonym "Elizabeth McNeill".

14
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Principal photography was completed in August 1984, but the
film was not released until February 1986.

15
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
Considered too explicit by its American distributor Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, 9½ Weeks was heavily edited for release in
the United States, where it was a box-office bomb, grossing $6.7 million on a $17 million budget.

16
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
It also received mixed reviews at the time of its release.

17
01:34:42,857 --> 01:34:48,857
However, its soundtrack sold well and the film itself became a huge success internationally in its unedited version,
particularly in Australia, Canada, France, Germany and the United Kingdom, grossing $100 million worldwide.

18
01:40:17,142 --> 01:40:23,142
It has also acquired a large fanbase on video and DVD
and has developed a cult following.

19
01:45:51,428 --> 01:45:57,428
The film explores themes of new york city, prostitute,
sexual obsession, fetish, eroticism.

